        {
          "path": "_m/c/b/t/g/voyageurs-national-park-wp/finger-bay-is-located-east-of-.jpg",
          "filename": "Finger Bay is located east of the Brule Narrows (Rainy Lake). Look for the Peary Lake Trailhead sign once you enter the bay (8ad0ebc9-b953-7a30-e43d-d56bb9c269c2).jpg",
          "caption": "Backcountry Campsite\nFinger Bay is located east of the Brule Narrows (Rainy Lake). Look for the Peary Lake Trailhead sign once you enter the bay.  Follow the trail for .3-mile to the canoe (48 31.4404, -092 46.1789).  To access the campsite, paddle the canoe south .4-mile to the site.  This campsite is also accessible from the Cruiser Lake Trail - .2-mile off the main trail where the canoe is not needed here to reach the campsite. The canoe is not accessible from the Cruiser Lake Trail.",
          "alt": "Backcountry Campsite\nFinger Bay is located east of the Brule Narrows (Rainy Lake). Look for the Peary Lake Trailhead sign once you enter the bay.  Follow the trail for .3-mile to the canoe (48 31.4404, -092 46.1789).  To access the campsite, paddle the canoe south .4-mile to the site.  This campsite is also accessible from the Cruiser Lake Trail - .2-mile off the main trail where the canoe is not needed here to reach the campsite. The canoe is not accessible from the Cruiser Lake Trail.",
          "width": 600,
          "height": 450,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "Public domain",
          "artist": "NPS",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Finger_Bay_is_located_east_of_the_Brule_Narrows_(Rainy_Lake)._Look_for_the_Peary_Lake_Trailhead_sign_once_you_enter_the_bay_(8ad0ebc9-b953-7a30-e43d-d56bb9c269c2).jpg",
